0226: the fused loop controller (GGML_OP_LOOP_CONTROL, 0221) for 1 .. 8 rows: a decode step, a draft's verify rows, a short prompt tail. That is the range the reference fuses (the vLLM-XPU Inkling port's loop_control.sycl, check_rows: 1 .. 8 rows) and the one 0221 left on the chain (it emitted the op for more than 8 rows only). 0221's kernel owns a work-group a Xe core, so at most 8 rows are ONE work-group: one core reading the control's 2.36 MB of weights. The small pair spreads the work as the reference does, in two launches (loop_control_small.cl): kernel_loop_control_gate, a work-group of 64 lanes a (row, half, output) - the half's down product and its sum of squares in one pass, the partial s_h*(Wd_h[r] . x_h) to a scratch [T][2][64] of the backend context - and kernel_loop_control_out, a lane a column - the two partials summed to g, the gain and forget products, tanh and the combine, T rows in one pass over the weight rows (row templates 1, 2, 4, 8). The switch stays GGML_OPENCL_LOOP_CONTROL: 1, f32 and all-layers now emit the op from one row; f32-t2 from two rows (one-row decode keeps the chain); f32-prompt is 0221's range (more than 8 rows); f32-onewg emits from one row and serves at most 8 rows with 0221's one-work-group kernel (the geometry's comparison arm); bf16 is unchanged (more than 8 rows, its own kernel). Unset, nothing changes: the chain is emitted node for node. ggml.h/ggml.c: ggml_loop_control_min_rows, ggml_loop_control_small_on, the plan's small launch. The model: n_tokens >= the switch's least row count, every other guard as it was. A second TAKEN line, WARN once a process: "loop_control: TAKEN opencl f32 small two-launch rows=.. gate_wg=.. out_tr=..". Reds through GGML_OPENCL_LOOP_CONTROL_OPTS=-DLOOP_CONTROL_RED=n: 1 - 4 as 0221's, 6 (the scratch's row step) and 7 (the tail row not stored) for 2 .. 8 rows. test-backend-ops: LOOP_CONTROL cases at 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8 rows (plain, a mix column's view; 6 rows is the verify of a 5-token draft), rows at a padded step (view=2) at 1 .. 57 rows, twins at 1, 2, 4, 6, 8 rows, perf cases op against chain at 1, 2, 4, 6, 8 rows.

